+`/v1/hs/set`
+-----------
+
+This endpoint sets or clears the vhost of an existing account, with the same semantics as `HS SET` and `HS DEL`. The request is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `accountName`: string, name of the account
+* `vhost`: string, the new vhost, or the empty string to clear it
+
+The response is a JSON object with fields:
+
+* `success`: whether the vhost was set or cleared
+* `errorCode`: string, optional, machine-readable description of the error. Possible values include: `INVALID_REQUEST`, `INVALID_VHOST`, `ACCOUNT_DOES_NOT_EXIST`, `ACCOUNT_UNVERIFIED`, `FEATURE_DISABLED` (vhosts are disabled, or DEFCON restricts them), `UNKNOWN_ERROR`.
+* `error`: string, optional, human-readable description of the failure if `errorCode` is `UNKNOWN_ERROR`
+
 `/v1/list`
